  "limits": "Finds only what stands 5 times above the noise of empty places in the picture of one visit or of all visits together, in at least one detector. A mover must move between visits (not within one: asteroids are averaged away), by less than 8 arcsec from one visit to the next (about 16 arcsec/yr for visits six months apart), and by more than about 1.2 to 3 arcsec/yr for 5 sigma, depending on brightness. Saturated stars are placed only to 1 to 2 arcsec. A brightness change must be at least 10 per cent (25 per cent for a saturated star's ring), seen at the same wavelength in at least 6 channels. Sources on the glow of a much brighter star are not tested, and a mover blended with catalogued neighbours is rejected. In nebulous young clusters, quote only changes seen the same way in two or more detectors. See docs/search.md.",
